# The three comment markers the lexer accepts, and why there are three: D §6.2 declares `--` and
# `/* … */`; 09-ui §7.4 registers Monaco with `lineComment: '#'`, which is what the editor's
# toggle-comment command inserts. All three round-trip verbatim.
-- A `--` line comment, per D §6.2.
/* A block comment, per D §6.2. */

# Two blank lines above this statement collapse to two; a run of nine would also collapse to two
# (D §6.4 caps blank_before at 0..2).
IF S1 = 1 THEN SHOW Q12                        # a trailing comment

-- The author's parentheses are preserved even though they change nothing: `(A AND B) OR C` and
-- `A AND B OR C` are the same AST, and stripping them from a rule about to be reviewed with a
-- client is hostile (D §6.4).
IF (S1 = 1 AND Q6 > 10) OR AGE >= 65 THEN SHOW Q12

-- Symbolic and numeric option references are both the author's choice, and both survive.
IF Q5 CONTAINS Q5.Apple THEN SHOW Q12
IF Q5 CONTAINS 1 THEN SHOW Q12
IF Q5 ANY OF [Q5.Apple, 3] THEN SHOW Q12
